  "name": "RAM 16x4 (teaching)",
  "category": "Memories",
  "prefix": "U",
  "description": "A small RAM to learn how a memory works: 16 words of 4 bits. A0-A3 select a word and Q0-Q3 always show it; while WE is 0 the word takes D0-D3 (write), when WE goes back to 1 it keeps them. The symbol lists the 16 words, the selected one marked (blue: read, red: write). No supply pins: the level (3.3 or 5 V) is a property; wire digital inputs and outputs, gates or a board's pins at the same level. A write needs WE to have been 1 first. Window > Memory Viewer shows and edits it while running.",
